                    "role": "assistant",
                    "content": "## Recruitment challenges for Canadian employers (2026)\n\n**Labour shortages persist.** Statistics Canada reported 512,000 job vacancies in Q3 2026, with health care, construction and skilled trades hardest hit [1]. The BDC notes that 55% of small businesses say hiring difficulties limit growth [2].\n\n**Time to fill is rising.** Average time to fill professional roles reached 44 days in 2026, up from 36 in 2022 [3].\n\n**Small firms lack HR capacity.** CFIB found that 6 in 10 owners do recruiting themselves, alongside running the business [4].\n\n**Why employers use recruiting firms.** Recruitment process outsourcing (RPO) adoption in Canada grew 18% year over year, driven by access to passive candidates, faster shortlists and lower cost per hire [5]."
